# Everything the image builds for itself, or has no business carrying.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile drops the host's node_modules on
# top of the one `npm ci` just installed on alpine. It happens to work today —
# both sets of platform binaries end up present and sharp picks the right one
# at runtime — but it is accidental rather than intended, and it is the same
# class of problem as the Prisma pin: a host artefact deciding what runs in the
# container.
node_modules
.next

# Local state and secrets. DATABASE_URL comes from the platform in production.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docker-compose.yml

# Nothing here is reachable from the running app.
.git
.github
.claude
.playwright-mcp
docs
deck
design
prototypes
build
_to_delete
*.md
!AGENTS.md

# Editor and OS litter.
.DS_Store
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
